From 72527905a38ed7a3f1748b2a557ae5670808bdaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:46:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/hevc: end the frame packing arrangement with its
 lifetime

The HEVC decoder exported the arrangement when a frame was decoded, from
state that stayed set until a later message or a cancellation. The
persistence flag only cleared it after the frame that carried it, so
with the flag set the arrangement lasted for the rest of the stream,
across any new coded layer-wise video sequence, and with the flag clear
a persistent message before it was lost as well.

H.265 D.3.16 says: "frame_packing_arrangement_persistence_flag equal to
0 specifies that the frame packing arrangement SEI message applies to
the current decoded frame only", and "equal to 1 specifies that the
frame packing arrangement SEI message persists for the current layer in
output order until any of the following conditions are true: A new CLVS
of the current layer begins. The bitstream ends. A frame picB in the
current layer in an access unit containing a frame packing arrangement
SEI message with the same value of frame_packing_arrangement_id and
applicable to the current layer is output for which PicOrderCnt( picB )
is greater than PicOrderCnt( picA )". The cancel flag "cancels the
persistence of any previous frame packing arrangement SEI message in
output order".

Do it as the H.264 and VVC decoders do: keep the message with its frame
and the sequence the frame belongs to, and resolve the arrangement when
the frame is output, so that it follows the output order. A frame shown
before the one that carries a message, such as a RASL picture before a
CRA picture, keeps the old arrangement; a new sequence clears it before
its first frame; a message with the persistence flag 0 applies to its own
frame only; temporal interleaving alternates the views. The state is
copied between frame threads with the other output state. Only the base
layer is resolved.

Link: https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24628
Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
